Extends perf-23/perf-31's leaf return-address elision (RiscV64ElideLeafRaSave) to methods whose only calls
are fast tail calls. A fast tail call leaves through `jalr zero` with RA untouched, so the callee returns
to our caller through the incoming RA and the method needs no RA save - but genComputeLeafRaElision
rejected every GT_CALL, fast tail calls included. It also rejected every compare shape
(GT_JCMP/LT/LE/GT/GE/MULHI), a rule carried over from .NET 10, where compare codegen used RA as a scratch
register; in .NET 11 compares use REG_ZERO or LSRA registers and mul-high uses an internal register, so
the rule is dropped and GT_RETURNTRAP and overflow-checked GT_MUL (which do write RA) are screened instead.
The decision moves into genFinalizeFrame, before frame layout, so a frameless method whose save is elided
reserves no RA slot, and a method with nothing to save and no locals gets no frame at all. The frameless
epilog's large-frame SP adjustment uses rsGetRsvdReg() (t6) instead of REG_SCRATCH (t0), which can hold an
indirect fast tail call target.
Same precondition as the knob: no GC thread suspension or return-address hijacking (zkVM targets only).

RISC-V64: elide the RA save (and the RA slot) in methods whose only calls are
fast tail calls; drop the stale .NET 10 compare screen. Requires the
upstream-perf profile (perf-23_frameless + perf-31_elide_leaf_ra_fp_guard) and
the RiscV64ElideLeafRaSave=1 knob that bflat passes for zkVM targets.

- genComputeLeafRaElision accepts GT_CALL nodes that are fast tail calls (a jump
  through jalr zero; the callee returns to our caller through the incoming RA).
- The GT_JCMP/GT_LT/GT_LE/GT_GT/GT_GE/GT_MULHI screen is removed: in .NET 11
  genCodeForCompare/genCodeForJumpCompare use REG_ZERO or LSRA registers and
  genCodeForMulHi an internal register. GT_RETURNTRAP (helper call) and
  overflow-checked GT_MUL (emitter uses RA) are screened instead.
- The decision moves into genFinalizeFrame, before frame layout, so a frameless
  method whose RA save is elided reserves no RA slot and, with nothing else to
  save and no locals, gets no frame at all (no addi sp pair). Framed methods keep
  the slot; the >2040-byte guard is applied after layout for them only.
- The frameless epilog's large-frame SP adjustment uses the reserved register
  (t6) instead of REG_SCRATCH (t0), which can hold a fast tail call target.

